prompts.environment:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: production-ready isometric dungeon TILE ATLAS PNG, true alpha transparency. This is a game asset sheet, not a poster, scene, UI mockup, or concept board.
Make exactly one 2048x1536 atlas: 4 columns by 3 rows of equal 512x512 invisible cells. Transparent gutters; NO drawn grid, labels, letters, numbers, captions, background, or checkerboard. Exactly ONE isolated sprite centered within each cell, no overlaps.
Art direction for Korean puzzle game "The Place the Hero Left": charming weathered dungeon repair workshop. Hand-painted stylized 2.5D game art, crisp confident silhouettes, soft chunky bevels, controlled detail visible when scaled down. Cool dark desaturated blue-grey stone, restrained moss green, aged bronze, bone ivory. Teal for restored/ready, dull amber for unfinished, coral-red for active hazard. Orthographic 2:1 isometric, camera looking down at 30 degrees, light upper left. NOT pixel art, not glossy plastic, not photoreal.
IMPORTANT every floor footprint uses identical diamond: cell-local left (48,304), top (256,200), right (464,304), bottom (256,408), with a shallow 18px stone side below. Entire sprite fits within 40px transparent padding. Tile is centered, never rotated differently. Do not draw extraneous cast shadows outside tile footprint. Tallest wall only 145px high above its tile so it won't hide puzzle paths.
Row 1 left-to-right:
1) ordinary clean flagstone floor, blue-grey square pavers, subtle seams;
2) same floor with a few fine cracks;
3) same floor with restrained moss along seams;
4) same floor with scrape marks and tiny chipped stones, fully walkable.
Row 2:
1) low solid masonry wall block exactly one tile footprint, chunky flat cap, visible two stone sides;
2) scattered destroyed stone rubble on same floor, low silhouette;
3) BROKEN spike-trap floor, missing bent spikes and clearly open damaged brass mechanism, muted amber;
4) REPAIRED INACTIVE spike-trap floor, neatly aligned dark sockets, all spikes fully retracted flush, brass rim.
Row 3:
1) ACTIVE spike-trap floor, six unmistakably tall raised ivory-metal spikes, small coral indicator accents;
2) EMPTY skeleton guard post, flat violet-grey carved shield emblem in floor, NO soldier;
3) CLOSED exit floor, low sealed bronze hatch, dim teal keyhole, no tall doorway;
4) READY exit floor, same hatch open revealing inviting restrained teal light, hatch lid low to one side.
All sprites align to same ground diamond, no outside shadows. True transparent background. No text, no watermarks. Clear state differences through shape as well as color.

